## SEVERITY / VERDICT
Blocker: any path beyond the 14, or a byte under `api/`, `.github`, `infra`, `scripts/`, `web/src` (other than the one test file), `playwright.config.ts` or a shared helper; a skip/removal/weakened assertion beyond the named `apiMode()` skip; the 297 cause not reproduced, contradicted, or a tier-1 trigger of Check 3 (STOP); the 297 test red at head, or green at base on a fresh showcase seed (premise); a refusal that does not fire (R1-R8) or a legitimate run refused or changed; a live spec red at head that passes at base's recorded behaviour; the two orders differ; the order check red; a customer left behind that the next spec reads; any red at head in the unit suite, typecheck, lint, build or `--check-shards` that base passes; a lost test name; a secret; a request that left loopback; a merge conflict; overlap with any live branch > 0. Major: any gate mutant of E1-E21 or S1-S2 that no row turns red (survivor); E22 not killed by the live probe; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (10 specs, 35 rows, 8 refusals, 32/2/0 per order, the three hashes' shape, 185 files / 2083, skip reason text); the instrument control not firing (the order comparison cannot see a planted dependence; the base 297 not red); a process or port of yours left behind; the load discipline broken without figures. Minor: an unclear refusal message; a source-text unit row that pins wording the live run does not need; the lost Demo-copy coverage in C-29 (Check 3d) if no assertion row was lost; `readiness-first-start` header claim untrue on the showcase seed; the "fresh seed per run" wording of the tickets not updated (Tuesday's to record); the playwright.config noise the builder reports (not in scope). **Notes (NOT failures):** no CI on a PR-less branch; the order check is an operator command (a CI job needs `.github/`, Tuesday's); the mode read cannot tell a showcase-OFF API on an old showcase database (disclosed; the skip is the safe direction); the B465 `Partner Dashboard` line; CodeQL not 